Package: omicsuite
Title: Analytical Pipelines for Biostatistics, Bioinformatics, and Computational Biology
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: person("Peekei", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "you@example.com")
Description: An extensible collection of high-level analytical pipelines for
    biostatistics, bioinformatics, and computational biology. Every pipeline
    in omicsuite follows the same contract: fit a model, run the diagnostic
    checks a careful methods section would include, render publication-ready
    'ggplot2' plots, and return a structured verdict table -- assumption
    checks, informational notes, and plain-language interpretation of the
    fitted effect -- rather than a bare point estimate. Currently includes
    Cox proportional hazards survival analysis with a full diagnostic suite:
    unadjusted-versus-adjusted comparison, global and covariate-level
    proportional hazards testing, influence diagnostics (dfbeta/dfbetas),
    functional form checks via martingale residuals, and hazard-ratio
    interpretation for every model term. Also includes a Bayesian
    hierarchical negative binomial mixed model pipeline for longitudinal
    RNA-seq count data, with gene-level partial pooling of the effect of
    interest, convergence diagnostics, posterior predictive checks, and a
    shrinkage plot. Also includes stochastic SIR/SEIR epidemic simulation via
    Gillespie's direct method, with an ensemble summary across realizations,
    final-size and peak-timing distributions, the implied basic reproduction
    number, and the probability of early stochastic extinction. Also
    includes multi-omics data integration via regularized generalized
    canonical correlation analysis, with per-block variance explained, a
    bootstrap-based loading stability check, and sample-score visualization
    across blocks. Also includes Kaplan-Meier survival curve estimation with
    a log-rank test, median survival with confidence intervals per stratum,
    and an optional parametric overlay for distributional comparison. Also
    includes competing risks analysis via cumulative incidence functions,
    Gray's test, and a Fine-Gray subdistribution hazard model. Every plot
    across every module carries its matching verdict note as a wrapped
    caption, so a figure alone -- not just the verdicts table -- carries its
    own interpretation. New pipelines are added following the same
    contract; see the package website for the current module list.
